{"ts": 1791256370.788384, "type": "step", "step": 8, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/evaluation.md", "section": "Evaluation"}, "output": "# Evaluating agents\n\n## pass@k vs pass^k\npass@k: any of k runs succeeds. pass^k: all k succeed. Reliability is what deployment needs.\n\n## Proxy vs direct measures\nA quiz score is a proxy. Retention a week later is closer to the thing itself.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.27095871991980863}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4740148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256370.7914739, "type": "step", "step": 9, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "Environment definition"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.27095871991980863}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4740148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256372.409157, "type": "step", "step": 10, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I found the key Friday-build requirements: (1) define the environment clearly in terms of state, observations, actions, and dynamics; (2) report pass^k on at least 3 seeds. The eval reading also suggests they care about reliability, not just one lucky run.\n\nSince you\u2019re stuck on eval, here\u2019s the main idea: pass@k means at least one of k runs succeeds, while pass^k means all k runs succeed. For a build/deployment story, pass^k is the stronger and more relevant claim.\n\nQuick check: can you tell me, in your own words, what numbers you\u2019d include if you ran 3 seeds with k attempts each?", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\n[activity] t=0 messages 2m", "t": 2, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.3342581511747653}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4940148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256374.086957, "type": "step", "step": 11, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "That\u2019s fine \u2014 let\u2019s make eval concrete.\n\nFor Friday, you\u2019ll want to report results across at least 3 seeds. A clean way to write it is:\n- Seed 1: result\n- Seed 2: result\n- Seed 3: result\n- Then a summary like: all 3/3 succeeded, so pass^3 = 1.0 for this setting (or 2/3, 1/3, etc., depending on outcomes).\n\nYour job is to show reliability, not just one good run.\n\nTry this: what would you say is the difference between \u201cpass@3\u201d and \u201cpass^3\u201d in one sentence each?", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=2 messages 2m", "t": 4, "activity": [{"t": 2, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.4185512871078879}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256375.671044, "type": "step", "step": 12, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can give you the exact wording to use, but I want to make sure it matches your build. For pass^k, the core answer is: you run the agent on k independent seeds and require success on all k runs; it\u2019s a stricter reliability metric than pass@k, which only needs one success among k runs.\n\nFor your writeup, you can say: \u201cWe report pass^k across 3 seeds to measure reliability: pass^k is the fraction of trials in which all k runs succeed.\u201d\n\nIf you want, I can help you turn that into a polished sentence for the evaluation section.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=4 messages 1m", "t": 5, "activity": [{"t": 4, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.424918879103789}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5940148929158049, "persistence": 0.4420657842665555, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256377.0213919, "type": "step", "step": 13, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Here\u2019s the shortest version you can use:\n\npass^k means you run k independent trials and **all k must succeed**. It is a stricter reliability metric than pass@k, which only needs **at least one** success among k runs.\n\nFor the writeup, a clean sentence is:\n\u201cWe report pass^k across 3 seeds to measure reliability: a trial counts as successful only if all k runs succeed.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=5 messages 1m", "t": 6, "activity": [{"t": 5, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.4312686500050733}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.6740148929158049, "persistence": 0.4120657842665555, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
